main_facts.json:$["0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3"]["glm-5.3"].trajectory.steps = `197`; .calls = `195`; .empty_agent_indices = `[]`. `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/agent/trajectory.json:$.steps[196].message` = `""`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/agent/trajectory.json:$.steps[196].tool_calls[0].function_name` = `"finish"`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/agent/trajectory.json:$.steps[196].tool_calls[0].arguments` = `{"message":"The LGA solver is written and the grant plan it emits is delivered. All twenty-five files sit under `/app/out` \u2014 the twenty-four data artifacts plus `/app/out/lgactl.py`, which is byte-for-byte the program that wrote them (re-running it reproduces every artifact identically). It uses only the Python standard library (`csv`, `hashlib`, `json`, `os`, `re`, `sys`, `unicodedata`) and reaches no network host. It reads only the record files of the corpus directory handed to it, writes only into the output directory, exits 0 on success, 2 on a wrong argument count or an absent corpus directory, and 3 when a required group (`runs-trace`, `selinux-allow`, `cap-units`, `grant-atoms`) is empty. `/app/data` is untouched, and nothing beyond the twenty-five named files is in `/app/out`.\n\nHow the work went. The solver reads all thirteen corpus encodings over the sharded groups, applies the five repairs before replay (never during), replays all 620 recorded runs \u2014 including the 390 unlabelled ones \u2014 through the four layers, and settles the plan in rounds. Every layer algebra was cross-checked against a from-scratch reimplementation: all 1860 PAM phase walks, all 620 capability ledgers, all 2721 seccomp decisions, all 620 domain transitions and SELinux refusals, the full admission ledger, the capability gaps and audit continuity, and the plan itself (rounds, cost choices, shrink and all 246 minimality witnesses) matched exactly. Two corpus-driven findings drove the result: the cost controls fix the multipliers at cap_bounding_add \u00d74 and seccomp_rule_add \u00d71 (both consistent pairs were settled and the cheaper shrunk plan kept), and 94 atoms are forbidden because, applied alone, each admits a must_deny run \u2014 those are excluded from the plan however cheap they are. The plan holds 246 atoms across 8 rounds; it admits 142 of the 146 must_admit runs, the remaining 4 are recorded as residuals with status nonconvergent (the cap of eight rounds was reached while they were still denied), and all 84 must_deny runs stay refused under the plan. Every one of the 246 atoms carries a witness run, the layer and the sequence at which the plan without it refuses that run. Determinism was proved two ways: a repeat run is byte-identical, and a corpus with every record re-listed in a different order produces byte-identical artifacts.\n\nThe closing figures, each worked out across the rows:\n\n- Total events the five repair rules corrected between them (an event corrected by two rules counts once for each): **2211** \u2014 arch 590, capability 370, number 588, perm 68, type 595.\n- Permissible atoms that repair no run that must be admitted: **1033** (1106 permissible atoms in the catalogue, of which 73 repair at least one must_admit run).\n- Mean cost of the atoms in the plan, rounded half-even to two decimal places: **3.38** (total effective cost 831 over 246 atoms).\n- Principals whose final disposition is granted: **84**."}`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].model_name` = `"glm-5.3"`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_tokens` = `27239570`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_cache_tokens` = `26979275`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_output_tokens` = `136362`; `0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_cost_usd` = `7.979`. main_facts.json:$["0b27b9dc-7985-54f1-a120-46e6810315a3"]["glm-5.3"].trajectory.error_hits has `5` flagged development/probe steps; these were reviewed as context, not equated with provider failures. No explicit terminal API/rate-limit/context/OOM event was established from the recorded messages. Cost null/agent_result cost 0 is not proof of free usage.

