mes for each\n\nr01 \u2014 `stages.stage_r01`: edge strengths summed row by row instead of once per declared sequence.\nr02 \u2014 `util.read_text`: byte order mark treated as part of the paper (the alias crosswalk lost its alias column and every binding). `util.read_delim`: quoted fields split on the separator inside them (a live identifier source was dropped). `loading.live_rows`: the frozen revision never applied, so the greatest revision was taken as live. `stages.window_grid` \u00d72: window starts read as offsets from the origin instead of a difference chain, and the live row taken against the scalar revision instead of each window's own frozen revision. `stages.context_grid`: the span chain started at zero instead of the origin.\nr03 \u2014 `stages._routine_cap`: the cap read from the routine layer before the memo cap table. `stages.stage_r03`: the window end treated as inclusive.\nr04 \u2014 `stages._absent`: a written zero treated as an absent field. `stages._layer_records`: one-shot remaining read from the journal instead of the snapshot. `stages.cooldown_floors`: the cooldown register read against the window grid's frozen revision instead of the snapshot's. `stages.resolve_policy` \u00d72: layers resolved in a fixed order instead of by the directive's ranks (action must outrank device), and the one-shot layer applied up to and including its expiry.\nr07 \u2014 `stages.stage_r07`: `key_settled_at` read the keys in the wrong order (tier before strength). `publish.run_chain`: the dependent tier taken over every expanded instance instead of the eligible ones.\nr09 \u2014 `stages.demand_of`: the first demand product carried unrounded into the second.\nr10 \u2014 `loading.read_workbook`: the live grid taken by sheet position instead of by key cell. `allocate._select` \u00d72: equality excluded from the pool fit test, and the scan stopped at the first misfit instead of considering the next candidate.\nr12 \u2014 `allocate.stage_r12` \u00d72: the round cap held inside the package (2) instead of the directive's 3, and each round offered the proposals alone instead of the holders together with the proposals.\nr13 \u2014 `allocate.stage_r13`: the one-shot consumed once per applying instance instead of once per override. `publish.render`: the next state's consumption taken from the first pass instead of the second.\nr14 \u2014 `allocate.stage_r14` \u00d72: the gate tested against the day's final value instead of the value in force strictly before the trigger, and kept proposals drawn from the pool twice. `publish.render`: `prior_cycle_mwh` taken from the last differing ledger row instead of the greatest cycle index.\n\nThese three symptoms are what the repairs close: the binding now binds against the live grid's zero ceilings and flags the true overruns (W05/DV-05, W06/DV-02); five one-shot overrides are now spent in the next snapshot (OV-006, OV-007, OV-008, OV-025, OV-901); and the round-2 binding now puts the incumbents back in the pool so nine instances are overturned for their fallbacks.\n\nOne judgement call worth flagging: the gate rule in r14 (\"the value written is not the required one\") I read as the value in force at the instance's trigger, not the key's final value \u2014 the two differ for readmission this cycle (a later write of the same value would otherwise have blocked RT-111#02)."}`; `b28ebc90-3080-5d41-9f01-e02549d3efaf/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].model_name` = `"glm-5.3"`; `b28ebc90-3080-5d41-9f01-e02549d3efaf/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_tokens` = `51215929`; `b28ebc90-3080-5d41-9f01-e02549d3efaf/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_input_cache_tokens` = `50889051`; `b28ebc90-3080-5d41-9f01-e02549d3efaf/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_output_tokens` = `224425`; `b28ebc90-3080-5d41-9f01-e02549d3efaf/trajectories/glm-5.3/run_1/trajectory_usage.json:$[0].trajectory_cost_usd` = `14.6