### 1C. v3.3 status (Ayush 27 Oct): proven test levers first, stated-rule levers paused
Our own runs 24-27 Oct: every stated-rule lever leaked to a fresh blind read (quiet branches tariff 226/226, sentinel 80/80; unique fit plus derived state tariff r2 301/301, sentinel r2 98/98; L11 tariff 3/3; breadth 40+ fuel-card exact; stated replay crash-recovery and scheduler 3/3 at 100), and stated limits handed over the core method (cold-chain, cleanroom, flood, tariff r3 bitset 397/397). What held:
- P-1 computational core with no stated decomposition parameter; the naive method times out at hidden scale and the strongest generic solver from the design blind times out or errs (sentinel r3: fresh blind 78.6%, probes tests 96.18 and 78.63).
- P-2 long stateful replay over hidden streams (match-replay 69.19).
- P-3 exact optimum on hidden instances larger than shipped (dispatch tests 35.64).
- P-4 behaviour and robustness checks (caldermoor `failed_run_leaves_no_partial_file`, wait_reserve).
- P-5 judge probe band (section 4; judge 40-75 down to 0-35 on caldermoor, sentinel, tariff).
New builds are siblings of P-1 to P-3 shapes. Stated-rule levers (L1-L11, S1, S3, S5, S6, H1-H9, T1-T4) are PAUSED, not discarded: no new hardening round relies on them until the lever audit (`prompts/drafts/lever_audit/PLAN.md`) checks each against delivered trajectories. A lever the audit finds not helpful is marked DISABLED here with its evidence; nothing is deleted.
- [v3.4: Ayush decision 4, 27 Oct] Law-1 filter. A test lever counts only when the strongest plausible solvers (the probe agent's program, every blind program, every generic solver in the kill test) lose by a valid but wrong document. Loss by timeout or crash does not count: a timeout tells the agent to fix its program and it recovers. Every kill table splits each solver's loss into WRONG / TIMEOUT / CRASH. P-1 and P-3 pass only with a WRONG stage (for example a plausible faster method that returns a feasible but non-optimal or wrongly carried figure). P-2 counts only with a stage where a plausible program passes the shipped history and is wrong on the hidden one (pass rate below 1 for plausible programs), not just slow.
- [v3.5: Ayush answer B, 27 Oct 20:10] Law-1 amended. A TIMEOUT or CRASH loss also counts ("hidden-scale loss") when all three hold: (1) no shipped input (shipped data, visible tests, any example in the docs) makes the plausible program time out or crash, so the agent sees no warning; (2) the limit it hits is stated: a runtime sentence in the docs (no method words), or the task's declared container memory for a crash; (3) the measured cost on plausible programs is 10-30% of positive test points and stays inside the lever checks: each lever corpus runs in its own call, so a timeout never costs non-lever checks. Evidence: sentinel harness attempts 5-7, real Opus lost 28 test points by timeout on hidden sizes and did not recover. A lever that fails (1)-(3) still needs a WRONG stage. Kill tables keep the WRONG / TIMEOUT / CRASH split and add a column 'shipped inputs fast: yes/no'.
- [v3.6: Ayush 27 Oct 22:30, new gate tests < 85, rubric < 85, final < 50; SUPERSEDED by the v3.7 bullet below] Overrides every 10-30% lever-cost figure (v3.5 condition 3, section 6, templates): a test lever now costs 25-40% of positive test points, and a plain first-write program and the all-but-one program aim at tests <= 75. Blind bar: each of the 3 fresh blind reads scores tests <= 80, its losses WRONG output or v3.5 hidden-scale loss. Judge: probe band with predicted probe mid 15-20. Overnight auto runs: the master may send "go" at DESIGN READY when the kill table passes (every generic solver and every blind program loses >= 15% of lever points, shipped inputs fast, reference <= 1/4 of the stated limit); otherwise Needs Ayush.
- [v3.7: Ayush 28 Oct "Target <40 now"; upgrade plan v2 C2, 29 Oct] Replaces the v3.6 bullet above. Plain first-write and all-but-one programs aim at tests <= 60. Blind bar: each of the 3 fresh blind reads scores tests <= 65 (none above 70), its losses WRONG output or v3.5 hidden-scale loss. Judge: probe band, predicted probe mid <= 20. DESIGN READY needs, in DESIGN.md: (a) predicted final = (predicted first-write tests + predicted judge mid)/2 <= 35 (5 points margin for the final spread; same-bytes spread, section 6 v3.4 bullet); (b) lever share >= 40% of positive test weight (if the lever is fully lost and all else passes, tests <= 60), with the held-out w5 tier >= 50% when the N2 shape is used; (c) blind ceiling: no blind program above tests 65; (d) verifier worst case <= 90% of the stated verifier limit; (e) the kill table rule (every generic solver and every blind program loses >= 15% of lever points by WRONG output, or v3.5 hidden-scale loss; shipped inputs fast; reference <= 1/4 of the stated limit) unchanged. Overnight go at DESIGN READY unchanged. Evidence: final < 40 needs tests + rubric < 80; our 10 valid gate runs mean tests 78.7, rubric 23.5, 1 below 40 (upgrade R3 FINDINGS:137).

Rejected as sources (do not plan on them): a cheap stateful rule beside the hard core with a silent redefinition (6d12f970 94 pts, cost_policy.md:8-13; RISKY IN-16, g1 GS:25); wrong-reading negatives (16 detectors fired 0 times, g4 GS:66-77; DL:54 TD8 "0 fired anywhere"); exact optimum with a stated method (80877080 core solved on 9 corpora, g4/C_80877080.md:9; cold-chain tests 100); odd carriers and format rules (g3 GS:79; LEAK_LIBRARY V0-7); mutation tiers alone (DL:52 "cheap for Opus").

How to combine: S1 or S2 as primary, plus S3, S5 or S6. Use S7 only with a CL-4 sentence. S8-S11 are garnish (4-5 points each).

